{"description":"Run `cargo check --message-format=json` and return compiler diagnostics as `file:line:col: level: message` lines. Use after an edit to see real errors instead of the whole build log. Fails open (missing cargo / timeout → a note, never an error).","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"level":{"description":"Which diagnostics to return (default: error).","enum":["error","warning","all"],"type":"string"},"package":{"description":"Restrict the check to one workspace package (`cargo check -p <package>`).","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"diagnostics"}
{"description":"Record or update the working plan for a multi-step task. No-op by design: it tracks intent only and executes nothing. ops: set (default) replaces the whole plan — resend the full list each call; update merges items by id (provided fields only, unknown ids appended, unlisted items kept); note records a decision/finding/assumption; next records the immediate next step; done marks one item done with evidence (and, for an item with done_when, asks for the note saying what was run and seen); handoff (top-level, called alone) resets the context to the run briefing plus `brief`. Durable: survives compaction and resume.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"brief":{"description":"op=handoff (≤4000 chars): what the fresh context needs — state, decisions, next steps.","type":"string"},"evidence":{"description":"op=done: a commit sha or task-N id the engine can verify.","type":"string"},"id":{"description":"op=done: the item id to mark done.","type":"string"},"items":{"description":"The whole plan, ordered. Required for op=set (replaced wholesale) and op=update (merged by id).","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"content":{"description":"Legacy alias of title.","type":"string"},"deps":{"description":"Item ids this one waits on.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"done_when":{"description":"What must be true to call this item done — a test name, a command and its expected result, an observable behaviour (≤400 chars). op=done on such an item asks for the evidence note; without one the completion is listed unverified. Empty clears it.","type":"string"},"id":{"description":"Stable item id (op=done/update/deps refer to it). Auto-assigned #1.. when omitted from op=set.","type":"string"},"parent":{"description":"Id of the item this one is a step of — one level of nesting; the parent shows its children's done count. Empty clears it.","type":"string"},"state":{"enum":["todo","doing","done","blocked","dropped"],"type":"string"},"status":{"description":"Legacy alias of state: pending|in_progress|completed.","type":"string"},"title":{"description":"One step. ('content' is also accepted.)","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"kind":{"description":"op=note: the note's kind.","enum":["decision","finding","assumption"],"type":"string"},"op":{"description":"set (default): replace the whole plan. update: merge the listed items by id, changing only the fields given. note: record a decision, finding or assumption. next: record what comes next. done: mark one item done with evidence. handoff: continue in a fresh context from `brief`.","enum":["set","update","note","next","done","handoff"],"type":"string"},"text":{"description":"op=note (≤1000 chars) / op=next (≤600 chars): the recorded text.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"plan"}
{"description":"JS (ES2020) function body; `tools.grep({pattern:'x'})` etc. return text, errors throw: read/grep/glob/bash/write/edit, deferred code tools; tools.call(name,args) for MCP. Only print() and the return value come back: batch loops/filters. No filesystem, network or imports.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"code":{"type":"string"},"timeout_s":{"description":"default 30","maximum":120,"type":"integer"}},"required":["code"],"type":"object"},"name":"run_code"}
